  "period_note": "Half-Yearly filing used as the Q2 data point, per project convention -- figures are H1-CUMULATIVE (1 January to 30 June 2025). BASIS BREAK FROM THE MAIN SERIES: Consolidated only, same as 2025_Q1.json (no Separate/Bank-only statement set is printed anywhere in this filing) -- flagged per the project's Solo-preference rule. Income-statement items are cumulative from 1 January 2025; the source also prints a discrete quarter-only column ('01 April to 30 June 2025': Net profit after tax -892,659,667, EPS -1.29) -- cross-checked: H1-cumulative NPAT -854,333,053 minus this dataset's own Q1 (2025_Q1.json) NPAT of 38,326,614 = -892,659,667, matching the discrete Q2 column exactly, confirming full internal consistency. EPS is plain 'Earnings per share (EPS)', not annualized. Consolidated Balance Sheet identity verified exactly (Total Liabilities 99,374,318,970 + Total Shareholders' Equity 7,908,912,483 = Total Assets 107,283,231,453). MAJOR RISK SIGNAL: Net interest income turned NEGATIVE this half (-290,807,407, cumulative; the discrete Q2-alone figure is even more negative at -797,619,348, meaning Q1 2025 alone was still positive at +506,811,941 -- consistent across this dataset's own 2025_Q1.json) as Interest paid on deposits and borrowings (3,725,905,907) grew faster than Interest income (3,435,098,500). Combined with a large increase in Specific provision (1,162,970,655 cumulative vs 75,815,156 in the same period of 2024, per the source's own comparative column -- a ~15x increase) and General provision turning strongly positive (241,148,474 vs 28,136,944 prior year), Total provision (D) rose to 1,483,516,964 (cumulative) from 246,871,251 in H1-2024, driving Net profit after tax from +105,541,064 (H1-2024) to -854,333,053 (H1-2025) -- Total shareholders' equity fell from 8,806,646,744 (31-Mar-2025) to 7,908,912,483 in this single quarter, and Retained earnings turned negative (-250,454,236). The bank's own FY2026-H1 filing (2026_Q2.json in this dataset) later explains this explicitly via a BSEC-mandated disclosure note: 'From 2025, Net Interest Income (NII) has a negative growth due to [a] non-performing loan (NPL) [event] in 2025 resulting decrease in interest income and transfer[s] to interest suspense of BDT 110.71 crore during the period January to June 2025.'",
